Sysmon Version History
======================

Version 0.94 - 2025-01-XX
-------------------------

Web UI Improvements:
  * Fixed critical 403 "object not found" errors by switching from STAT to STATO
    command (hostname vs unique_name mismatch eliminated)
  * Added daemon information display (version, uptime) to dashboard
  * Implemented session logger for all sysmon protocol operations
  * Added session log and error display to admin page with auto-refresh
  * Created dual-view host display system:
    - Comparison view: ultra-compact grid showing 30+ hosts
    - Table view: sortable detailed table with check statistics
    - Toggle button to switch between views instantly
  * Made UI extremely compact to show more hosts per screen
  * Added hover tooltips with full host details in comparison view
  * Fixed dashboard layout bug (content no longer shifts during refresh)
  * Reduced all connection timeouts from 30s to 5s for responsive UI
  * Eliminated all ReadString() error handling bugs (Go idiom fixes)
  * All views now prominently display hostnames (not just IP addresses)

Protocol and Communication:
  * Fixed web-UI protocol handling to support all sysmon response codes
    (333, 403, 444) instead of blindly parsing everything as XML
  * Added structured response parsing with readSysmonResponse() helper
  * Implemented proper error detection and recovery for protocol operations
  * Fixed XML parsing to handle EOF correctly (process line before checking error)
  * Added QUIT command to cleanly close connections (eliminates connection resets)

Daemon Improvements:
  * Fixed ICMP race condition where responses processed after timeout checks
    (reordered event loop to call handle_icmp_responses before service_checks)
  * Increased ping timeout from 1 second to 2 seconds to reduce false negatives
  * Fixed NULL pointer bug in textfile.c (filename checked before use)
  * Fixed incomplete XML send on connection errors (do_send_xml returns status)
  * Added SEND_OR_ABORT macro for reliable XML transmission
  * Implemented config minnumfailures directive:
    - Minimum consecutive failures before host appears in status file
    - Reduces false alarms from transient failures
    - Default is 1 (show after first failure)
  * Implemented config flaptime directive:
    - Keep host showing as green for N minutes after recovery
    - Prevents "flapping" appearance in status output
    - Default is 0 (disabled)

Security and Privilege Dropping:
  * Added statustempdir configuration directive for privilege-dropped daemon
  * Allows daemon to write status files when running as unprivileged user
  * Created dedicated temp directory support for status file generation
  * Documented privilege dropping setup in README and man pages

Documentation:
  * Added comprehensive sysmon protocol documentation
  * Updated sysmon.conf.man with statustempdir directive
  * Added setup instructions for privilege dropping
  * Documented all configuration directives with examples
  * Improved man page formatting and clarity
  * Added minnumfailures and flaptime directive documentation to man page
  * Converted all markdown documentation to plain ASCII text in docs/

Bug Fixes:
  * Fixed perror() calls behind debug checks to reduce log noise
  * Fixed NFD button visibility (only shows when authentication configured)
  * Eliminated browser console errors for admin endpoints
  * Fixed Chart.js layout issues causing content to grow/shift
  * Corrected timeout handling throughout web-UI backend

Performance:
  * Web-UI now loads hosts quickly without wasted API calls
  * Eliminated hundreds of failed SHOWOBJ requests
  * Reduced protocol overhead with proper command usage
  * Session logging replaces stderr output for better observability

Version 0.93 and Earlier
------------------------

See docs/README and git history for earlier changes.

Wishlist for Future Versions
-----------------------------

Priority Items:
  * Multiple textfile outputs (by groups, by state)
  * Per-host pageinterval configuration
  * SNMP custom up/down messages
  * SNMP OID comparison and custom error descriptions
  * State persistence across daemon restarts (config savestate)
  * SNMP query aggregation to reduce network overhead

Nice to Have:
  * Enhanced DNS checks documentation
  * SNPP notification support
  * Additional authentication backends (htpasswd, etc.)
  * Curses client improvements

Completed:
  * Web UI with authentication - DONE (FastCGI-based web-UI in web-ui/)
  * IRC daemon check - DONE (basic ircd check implemented)
  * Documentation - ONGOING (continuous improvements)
  * Paused host data visibility - DONE (visible in web-UI)
  * Configurable flaptime - DONE (v0.94: config flaptime directive)
  * Minimum failure count before yellow/txt - DONE (v0.94: config minnumfailures)
